## 3. `LearningRecordsPage.vue` — records fetch and pending counts

**Fetch:** `GET /api/v1/learning-records?...` with optional `branch_id`, `student_name`, `teacher_id`, `status`; always `sort=session_date`, `per_page=200`. Teachers do not auto-set `filters.teacher_id` in code — listing is expected to be scoped by the backend for the logged-in teacher.

```1511:1535:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/LearningRecordsPage.vue
const fetchRecords = async () => {
  try {
    const token = await getToken();
    if (!token) return;

    const params = new URLSearchParams();
    if (props.branchId) params.set('branch_id', props.branchId);
    if (filters.student_name) params.set('student_name', filters.student_name);
    if (filters.teacher_id) params.set('teacher_id', filters.teacher_id);
    if (filters.status) params.set('status', filters.status);
    params.set('sort', 'session_date');
    params.set('per_page', '200');

    const res = await fetch(`/api/v1/learning-records?${params.toString()}`, {
      headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}` }
    });

    if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Fetch failed');

    const data = await res.json();
    records.value = data.data || [];
```

**Counts** (computed from `records` after load):

```770:772:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/LearningRecordsPage.vue
const pendingCount = computed(() => (records.value || []).filter(r => r.Status === 'pending' || r.Status === 'changes_requested').length);
const changesRequestedCount = computed(() => (records.value || []).filter(r => r.Status === 'changes_requested').length);
const approvedCount = computed(() => (records.value || []).filter(r => r.Status === 'approved').length);
```

**Teacher UI nuance:** The teacher tab “待��核” filters to **`Status === 'pending'` only** (not `changes_requested`). “需修改” uses `changes_requested` and shows `changesRequestedCount` on the tab. Director “�列” uses `pendingCount`, which **includes both** pending and changes_requested.

```708:717:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/LearningRecordsPage.vue
const filteredRecords = computed(() => {
  let list = records.value || [];
  if (isTeacher.value) {
    if (teacherFilterTab.value === 'changes_requested') {
      list = list.filter(r => r.Status === 'changes_requested');
    } else if (teacherFilterTab.value === 'approved') {
      list = list.filter(r => r.Status === 'approved');
    } else if (teacherFilterTab.value === 'pending') {
      list = list.filter(r => r.Status === 'pending');
    }
```

