## 4. `/home/admin/frontend/src/lib/classSessionsApi.js`

**Exports:**

- **`normalizeClassSessionsPayload(json)`** — flattens API JSON into `items` and `byClass` (key = `student_class_id`), with normalized fields (`session_date`, `start_time`, `end_time`, `learning_record_*`, etc.).
- **`fetchClassSessions(opts)`** — `GET /api/v1/class-sessions?` with optional `branchId`, `studentClassId`, `studentClassIds` (comma-separated, chunked at 60 IDs), `teacherId`, `studentId`, `start`, `end`, `per_page`; merges chunk results if needed.

```48:77:/home/admin/frontend/src/lib/classSessionsApi.js
async function fetchClassSessionsSingle({
  token, branchId, studentClassId, studentClassIds,
  teacherId, studentId, start, end, perPage = 2000,
} = {}) {
  const params = new URLSearchParams();
  if (branchId) params.set('branch_id', String(branchId));
  if (studentClassId) params.set('student_class_id', String(studentClassId));
  if (Array.isArray(studentClassIds) && studentClassIds.length) {
    params.set('student_class_ids', studentClassIds.map((id) => Number(id)).filter((id) => id > 0).join(','));
  }
  if (teacherId) params.set('teacher_id', String(teacherId));
  if (studentId) params.set('student_id', String(studentId));
  if (start) params.set('start', String(start));
  if (end) params.set('end', String(end));
  params.set('per_page', String(perPage));

  const res = await fetch(`/api/v1/class-sessions?${params.toString()}`, {
    headers: {
      'Accept': 'application/json',
      ...(token ? { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}` } : {}),
    },
  });
  // ...
  return normalizeClassSessionsPayload(json);
}
```

For a **TeacherHomePage**, reusing **`fetchClassSessions`** with `teacherId` (if the API supports it) may align with `AttendancePage`’s date-range style; `LearningRecordsPage` instead uses **`studentClassIds`** from `student-classes` without passing `teacherId`.

---

## 5. Composables under `/home/admin/frontend/src/composables/`

Only **`course-management/`** exists, with three modules — all geared to **CourseManagement** (sessions display, edit flow, reschedule/makeup), not a generic teacher dashboard:

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `/home/admin/frontend/src/composables/course-management/useSessionEditFlow.js` | Session edit modal, status transitions, wiring to `CourseManagement` |
| `/home/admin/frontend/src/composables/course-management/useCourseSessionsDisplay.js` | Loads completed session dates via `fetchClassSessionsFn`, expands dates in UI |
| `/home/admin/frontend/src/composables/course-management/useRescheduleAndMakeup.js` | Reschedule/makeup modals and slot logic |

There is **no** shared composable today for `LearningRecordsPage` schedule or `AttendancePage` pending sessions; those patterns live inline in the page components.

---

**Summary for TeacherHomePage:** Reuse **`fetchClassSessions`** from `/home/admin/frontend/src/lib/classSessionsApi.js` and the same **`GET /api/v1/student-classes`** + **`GET /api/v1/learning-records`** patterns as `LearningRecordsPage`; for “待��名” parity, mirror **`fetchPendingSessions`** (`/api/v1/class-sessions` + `scheduled` filter, no `branch_id` for teachers). Confirm in Laravel that teacher-scoped routes filter by the authenticated user when `branch_id` / `teacher_id` are omitted.

